WEBVTT

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:39.100
There's no doubt now the Jap shot down the clipper to get Marling in his party.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:40.340
It looks that way.

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:43.470
And if he's alive, they'll torture the man in secret out of him.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.440
In that case, I'd rather see him dead.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.460
That secret can mean the difference between winning and losing.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:49.200
I know.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.290
And I don't believe in miracles.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:52.740
But I wish one would happen.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:01:59.710
First visit to the outside.

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:02.330
It's not a very pleasant one, has it, Marling?

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:04.760
Well, surely it hasn't been monotonous.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:07.770
Shot down by Japs, imprisoned in a sub-tender,

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:09.870
and finally escaping in this eggshell.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:14.310
My chief regret is that we had to leave Martin and Wingley

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:15.830
aboard the Japanese ship.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.710
Jack had some wild scheme. He'd take over the ship's radio

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:21.500
and warn Pearl Harbor that the Japs mean to attack

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.660
without declaring war.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.180
C-4 calling headquarters.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.440
The Starling's flying the jet flag now.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:37.240
Please, and stand by correction.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.750
There's no use of us staying here to commit hara-carry wing.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.310
The same idea occurred to me.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:05.870
Let's go.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:28.300
As though Jack did what he promised, but at what he cost to himself.

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:35.210
We must have had a chance to jump. I'm glad we followed them.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:38.520
Hey, wait! That looks like our sailboat!

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:42.520
Hey, I can't make it!

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:52.820
Get your head, shoulders, and squiggly!

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:28.680
luck was with us, and we made it.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:29.970
I guess we...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.400
We both believe in miracles now, eh?

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.000
And how, 100%.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:33.320
Right.

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:35.070
Now about this treaty.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.170
Of course, I have authority to sign it,

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.570
but I admit that I'm rather hazy about it.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:42.160
Ma Ling, the most important person rescued

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:44.240
through Captain Martin's bravery and cleverness,

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:47.360
is governor of a Chinese province over against the Himalayas.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.400
Oh, you deserve the praise, Captain Martin.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:51.020
Yes, Captain Wing.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:53.520
Well, sir, a secret route from China to India

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.580
runs through Mandan, Ma Ling's state.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.440
Is that fact or fairy tale?

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.840
If Ma Ling says it's a fact, it's a fact.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.800
Then why hasn't he given it to China?

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:04.670
His people want no traffic for the outside world.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:08.000
And he demands guarantees the road be closed after the war.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.900
China and Great Britain have already promised.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:11.850
Why does he want the United States to sign?

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:13.760
Well, up until yesterday, he wanted

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:15.660
us to sign as a disinterested nation.

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:17.870
Now, of course, he wants us to sign as an ally.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:19.030
I see.

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:21.690
Well, as vital as this is, do you

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:24.690
suppose you could persuade Ma Ling to postpone our conference?

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.320
Yesterday's treachery has left me swamped.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.970
As a matter of fact, he rather expects postpone.

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:33.380
Well, that ends my part in the matter.

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.220
Now for the good old USA and the uniform.

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:37.100
I'm sorry, but I have orders to the contrary.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.960
You're to stay with Ma Ling as his special envoy

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.600
until he is safely back in Mandan.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:43.140
But America needs aviators.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.200
And I want to drop some eggs on those Japs.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:46.620
We need you more on this job.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.540
Ma Ling himself suggested it.

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:50.530
Well, those are orders.

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:54.020
Will you detail some policemen to stay in guard until we leave?

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:55.540
Worried over the Black Samurai?

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.100
They'll go to any length to kill him before he signs that treaty.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:05:59.970
Well, I'll do it if it'll relieve you.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.680
But after yesterday, all Japs are under control.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.090
And that should include any member of the Black Samurai.

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:12.930
A jeweler in town.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.500
What on earth do you want a jeweler for?

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:18.210
Marling's been so nice about letting me take pictures

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.210
and giving me news scoops.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:20.840
I'd like to show him I appreciate it.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:22.200
It's a nice thought.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.060
Why don't you ask the desk?

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:25.100
That's a good idea.

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:29.810
Hello?

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:32.040
Would you give me the desk, please?

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:35.840
Hello?

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.520
I wonder if you could recommend a reliable jeweler.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:41.100
What was that?

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:42.290
Blinker?

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:44.280
John Blinker?

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:47.100
Is he a phone?

00:06:49.390 --> 00:06:49.830
Thank you.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.400
John Blenker at Crest 4565.

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:05.630
Did you find one?

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:07.080
You never can tell.

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:07.990
I'm in Briggs.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:12.800
Hotel Hilo.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:14.380
D. Gertrude Miller?

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:17.220
I'm on Teufel.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:19.100
Yes, Fr. Lime.

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:20.750
I mean, yes, Miss Miller.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:22.300
How can I serve you?

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:26.320
I wonder if you could bring over some samples of your work to the hotel sometime today.

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:28.890
Within the hour?

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:33.090
That would be fine. I'll be expecting you.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:34.830
Bye.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.100
You sound stupid enough to be really good.

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:45.920
I'm Van Tiefel, the head of the German Black Samurai.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:52.280
Work for me, Johan Blanke.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:05.030
It's all beautiful.

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:08.370
Janet, this would look lovely on you.

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:10.680
Do you mind if I tried them on?

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:11.900
Certainly not.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:16.680
What I really want is a duplicate of this

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.490
for a friend who's admired it.

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:28.720
Can you make a replica of it?

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:29.970
Yes, sir.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.460
I believe I can duplicate it.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:34.060
It must be able to stand close examination.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.280
I have an artist friend, an oriental named Han Po.

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:39.860
He will make you a perfect facsimile.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.000
Don't you do your own artwork?

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:44.540
I am an artist, not a goldsmith.

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:46.070
I used to be an actor.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:50.830
Now I design, and my work is always satisfactory.

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:51.800
Good.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:53.340
Keep the locket.

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:55.310
I will give you a check on account.

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:09.320
Is Madame interested in buying?

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:13.030
I don't think so. I was just indulging in a little wishful thinking.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:16.500
You should change your mind. Here's my car.

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:17.290
Thanks.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.550
You'll have to hurry. We may only be here a couple of days.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:37.880
Thank you. It'll be finished before you expect it.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.200
Stand guard until relieved.

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.520
Don't let anyone enter without first checking with us.

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:12.320
Yes, sir, I understand.

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:14.850
Who is it?

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:15.910
Wing and Jack.

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:21.250
Let it go off duty now, Tommy.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:22.470
We've brought a couple of police guards.

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:26.730
Look, Draxon's in my country's anxious to sign the treaty,

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:28.030
but has asked for a day's delay.

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:29.970
Yesterday's bombing raid has thrown...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.640
and all government officers in a turmoil.

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:33.180
It could not be otherwise.

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:36.930
And patience has long been a virtue of my people.

00:10:38.090 --> 00:10:39.610
Is there anything we can do for your Excellency?

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:41.270
Nothing, thank you.

00:10:42.020 --> 00:10:43.320
Well, we'll get the girls and have some lunch.

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:04.900
That is my unworthy name.

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:08.340
I was right.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:10.680
If you are from the police, I have done nothing.

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:12.420
I am not from the police.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:14.720
Are we alone?

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:16.980
No one can see nor hear.

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:21.780
You are listed as a loyal subject of Japan.

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:24.660
Who are you to come to my poor shop and accuse me of being Japanese?

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:29.970
Line of the black, sir.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:34.920
Yes, I am a loyal subject of Japan.

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:39.000
Then you would be willing to undertake a mission against our enemies.

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:40.410
You have only to order.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:46.100
It will be dangerous. It may even cost you your life.

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:47.770
I am willing to take that risk.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:50.020
I knew I could count on you.

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:54.460
Close the shop. Lower the blind. We must have privacy.

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:22.740
Here, too dark. Nose a little out of proportion.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:25.250
That can be remedied.

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.580
Chief sent us up to relieve you.

00:12:50.730 --> 00:12:52.370
We're not supposed to go off duty yet.

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:54.630
He said he wanted all regular police on street patrol.

00:12:55.110 --> 00:12:56.550
We're on special just for this case.

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:57.780
Okay.

00:13:13.150 --> 00:13:14.370
Where do you want this foot?

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:16.260
I really do not know.

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:18.070
May I ask what it's in?

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:22.450
Sit down, put it in the box.

00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:52.610
I wonder what happened to the two guards?

00:13:58.230 --> 00:13:58.630
Oh, Link!

00:13:59.270 --> 00:13:59.970
Girls, you better stay.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.900
See what you can do for Wu-Tan.

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:08.170
I had a... something like this would happen.

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:10.510
You were ordered not to leave that door until you were relieved.

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:12.230
We were relieved before our shift was up.

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:14.910
Seemed funny, so I checked and found the chief hadn't sent any relief.

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:16.150
How did this happen?

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:17.050
We have no idea.

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:19.500
Several men delivered a large box.

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:23.330
When I asked them what it was, they struck me over the head with a gun.

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:24.480
I...

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:36.260
Marling.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:46.360
Man is not Marling.

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:47.360
Wait a minute.

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:48.240
Don't phone headquarters.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:50.370
Why do you say this man's not Marling?

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:52.890
That ring.

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:54.630
Well, it's still there.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:56.840
Yes, but it is reversed.

00:14:57.970 --> 00:14:58.870
You would never do that.

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:01.240
It has a religious significance.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.020
It doesn't seem possible.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:05.510
This man's a perfect double for Marling.

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:06.670
Not quite.

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:12.800
The gentleness in Marling's face is none in his.

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:14.510
I don't get it at all.

00:15:14.670 --> 00:15:15.410
I'm beginning to.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:17.880
They wanted Marling so they could question him

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:19.020
and didn't want us to look for him.

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:20.660
So they brought this man here in a box

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:22.280
and killed him before they took Marling away.

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:23.980
Have you any idea who this man is?

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:26.220
No, but there's a chance he has a police record.

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:27.140
Check his fingerprints,

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:28.680
and if you find out anything, phone us.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:29.260
Yes, sir.

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:35.630
The police must be mistaken.

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:39.240
No human being can think of a plan so cruel, not even a Jap.

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:41.190
Haven't you forgotten something, Trudy?

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:43.860
How about Forlan von Teufel or the Black Samurai?

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:44.600
Why, they...

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:46.090
Excuse me.

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:51.600
Speaking.

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:53.650
Oh, wait a minute.

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:54.680
What's that name again?

00:15:56.210 --> 00:15:58.440
Han Poe.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.680
I'm going to meet the police down at his shop.

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:16.480
I'm going along too. Coming, Trudy?

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:18.720
No, I think I've had all I can stand for one day.

00:16:41.868 --> 00:16:45.708
You have heard no doubt of burning bamboo splints under the fingernails.

00:16:46.604 --> 00:16:49.564
As a means of securing secrets from a stubborn prisoner?

00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:53.380
One of the higher of the few Japanese artists.

00:16:53.676 --> 00:16:54.236
I believe.

00:16:56.236 --> 00:16:59.236
effective one.

00:17:06.012 --> 00:17:06.512
Yes?

00:17:07.676 --> 00:17:09.676
is further than Typhoon.

00:17:10.204 --> 00:17:11.044
Yes, I have him here.

00:17:12.220 --> 00:17:12.440
All right.

00:17:13.596 --> 00:17:13.996
Police!

00:17:15.836 --> 00:17:17.836
Don't worry, they won't find him here.

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:20.660
I have a car outside. I'll take him to my place in the hills.

00:17:35.436 --> 00:17:37.196
They had them here, and we're about to torture them.

00:17:37.316 --> 00:17:38.216
They must have just left.

00:17:38.256 --> 00:17:39.256
They didn't get out the front way.

00:17:39.356 --> 00:17:40.056
I'll try the back.

00:17:43.116 --> 00:17:44.536
And Poe was only small, Fry.

00:17:45.452 --> 00:17:48.032
If only we had one clue to some of the higher-ups.

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:49.140
Tempo.

00:17:49.612 --> 00:17:51.432
I knew I'd heard that name before today.

00:17:51.792 --> 00:17:53.132
The jewelry designer mentioned him.

00:17:53.212 --> 00:17:54.052
What jewelry designer?

00:17:54.212 --> 00:17:55.872
The one in the hotel recommended to Trudy.

00:17:56.428 --> 00:17:59.128
He said Han Poe could make a locket she wanted.

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:03.240
This doesn't look like a goldsmith's shop.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.420
Do you remember his name?

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:06.460
No.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:08.590
Yes, I do.

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:10.490
He gave me his card.

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:14.870
There was a car pulling out of the alley, but it was too far ahead.

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:17.980
The policeman is trying to commandeer a car to follow, but it looks hopeless.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.060
Janet's found a clue. Come on, I'll explain on the way.

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:52.050
and said they had jewelry designer maybe mixed up in it.

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:54.020
What, Blanker?

00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:57.160
Yes, the boys are on their way to his house now to question him.

00:18:57.890 --> 00:18:59.970
We should have got sight of him by now if we're on the right line.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:00.140
Please.

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:02.640
a dozen roads to his place.

00:19:06.236 --> 00:19:06.736
Excuse me.

00:19:07.164 --> 00:19:08.604
I think I'll go and lie down for a minute.

00:19:09.084 --> 00:19:10.304
Too much excitement, I guess.

00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:25.240
Select the car we saw leave the alley.

00:19:27.068 --> 00:19:27.728
Certainly does.

00:19:37.228 --> 00:19:38.108
This is the car we want on.

00:19:38.188 --> 00:19:40.348
Notice how he picked up speed when he spotted us?

00:19:46.284 --> 00:19:46.584
Yes.

00:19:48.588 --> 00:19:49.588
Take a little louder, please.

00:19:51.724 --> 00:19:52.664
Pauline Von Diver.

00:19:53.292 --> 00:19:54.092
You must act quickly.

00:19:55.372 --> 00:19:57.032
Blanca is on his way home with the prisoner.

00:19:57.804 --> 00:19:59.944
Martin and his two friends are following fast.

00:20:00.410 --> 00:20:02.500
I understand, Fräulein, and thank you.

00:20:11.510 --> 00:20:12.960
Get to the bridge.

00:20:13.460 --> 00:20:14.600
Let Blenker's car pass.

00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:17.350
Then use the emergency rig to stop the one following.
